course: dictionary
lesson: 5711
title: Longevity: a long life, or a long time lasting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Longevity is a noun. It means living a long life. «Tortoises are famous for their longevity» tells you that tortoises are known for living many years.
explain: Longevity can also mean lasting for a long time, like the longevity of a building or a TV show. Ask yourself: is the thing alive? If it is alive, the word is about a long life. If it is not, it is about lasting a long time.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The secret of longevity» and «known for its longevity» both sit near words like famous, secret and known. These phrases tell you the word is a big, important idea.
explain: In China, people eat «chángshòumiàn» on birthdays, especially grandparents' birthdays. These are longevity noodles. You do not cut or bite them short, because long noodles stand for a long life.
fact: Longevity means living a long life.
fact: Longevity can also mean lasting for a long time, like a building or a TV show.
fact: Longevity is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «their longevity», not «their longevities».
fact: «Chángshòumiàn» are longevity noodles eaten on birthdays, especially by grandparents.
fact: You do not cut the noodles short, because long noodles mean long life.
exercise: «Tortoises are famous for their longevity.» What does longevity mean here? | *Living a long life | Hiding in the sand | Being very fast
exercise: Which sentence uses longevity to mean lasting for a long time? | The children ran to the park | The dog was barking loudly | *The longevity of the old bridge means it has stood for over a hundred years
exercise: Find and copy the word from this sentence that shows the noodles stand for a long life: «Grandma's birthday noodles are long, so nobody cuts them short.» | *long | birthday | grandma's | noodles
test: «The secret of longevity» is a phrase about which idea? | How to win a race | *How to live a long life | How to cook noodles quickly
test: «The bridge is known for its longevity, because it has lasted over two hundred years.» What does longevity mean? | Being very bright | Being very heavy | *Lasting for a long time
exam: Which phrase means the secret to living a long life? | the speed of a car | a short holiday by the sea | *the secret of longevity
